T*
(7. Future Perfect Continuous) Tj
T*
(Se forma con will have been + verb-ing y destaca la duración de una actividad hasta un punto) Tj
T*
(futuro.) Tj
T*
(By next June, I'll have been studying English for three years.) Tj
T*
(Para el próximo junio, llevaré tres años estudiando inglés.) Tj
T*
(Cómo elegir la forma correcta) Tj
T*
(Situación | Forma recomendada |) Tj
T*
(Decisión inmediata | will |) Tj
T*
(Intención previa | going to |) Tj
T*
(Plan organizado | Present Continuous |) Tj
T*
(Horario oficial | Present Simple |) Tj
T*
(Acción en progreso en el futuro | Future Continuous |) Tj
T*
(Acción completada antes de una fecha | Future Perfect |) Tj
T*
(Duración hasta una fecha futura | Future Perfect Continuous |) Tj
T*
(Errores frecuentes) Tj
T*
(? I will to call you. ? I will call you.) Tj
T*
(? I going to study. ? I'm going to study.) Tj
T*
(? I'm meet him tomorrow. ? I'm meeting him tomorrow.) Tj
T*
(? By Friday I will finish already. ? By Friday, I'll have finished.) Tj
T*
(Ejercicios) Tj
T*
(The phone is ringing. I ________ \(answer\) it.) Tj
T*
(Look at those clouds! It ________ \(rain\).) Tj
T*
(I ________ \(meet\) Laura tomorrow at 6; we arranged it yesterday.) Tj
T*
(The train ________ \(leave\) at 07:30.) Tj
T*
(This time tomorrow, we ________ \(fly\) to New York.) Tj
T*
(By next week, she ________ \(finish\) the project.) Tj
T*
(By 2030, he ________ \(work\) here for twenty years.) Tj
T*
(I think people ________ \(use\) more renewable energy in the future.) Tj
T*
(Soluciones) Tj
T*
(will answer) Tj
T*
(is going to rain) Tj
T*
(am meeting) Tj
T*
(leaves) Tj
T*
(will be flying) Tj
T*
(will have finished) Tj
T*
(will have been working) Tj
T*
(will use) Tj
T*
(Reto final) Tj
T*
(Escribe siete frases sobre tu futuro intentando usar una forma diferente en cada una: will,) Tj
T*
(going to, Present Continuous, Present Simple, Future Continuous, Future Perfect y Future) Tj
T*
(Perfect Continuous.) Tj
T*
(Sigue estudiandoCompara presente, pasado y futuro para dominar el sistema verbal completo.) Tj
T*
